{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Celebrating Christmas"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Family Gatherings"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le18ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We have different ways of talking about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We often use <span class=\"italic\">going to (+ infinitive)</span>, the <span class=\"italic\">present continuous (to be + -ing)</span> or <span class=\"italic\">will (+ infinitive)</span>. <br><br>  The structure we use depends on the function of what we want to say, whether we are talking about arrangements, plans, predictions. <br><br>  You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I'll help.</span> <br><br>  You use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> to talk about intentions.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are we going to open our gifts? <br> I'm going to have to rest a bit before I eat any more.</span>  <br><br>  The <span class=\"italic\">Present Continuous</span> tense is used to talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span>  <br> <span class=\"italic\">We're having our yearly family gathering tonight.</span>  <br><br>  You use the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about schedules or timetables in the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">The restaurant closes for 2 days at Christmas.</span> "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying What is Necessary"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you say what is necessary to follow advice, you use <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">going to have to</span>.</br> <span class=\"italic\">Have got to</span> focuses on now and in the future. <span class=\"italic\">I'm going to have to</span> focuses on the future alone. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to have to rest a bit before I eat any more."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to work tomorrow?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to have to hide them!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timewise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with respect to time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Britain is 5 hours ahead timewise. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at Christmas dinner."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "yearly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "every  year "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We're having our yearly family gathering tonight. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to envy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to want what others have"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone will envy me! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to chat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to talk"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I always chat with my family on Christmas morning. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to clean up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put away things; wash the dishes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's clean up and then go out! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Name two holidays when you don't have to work or go to school."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe what you have to do before the holiday starts to get ready."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner what food you prepare or help prepare."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner what you have to buy."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about two holidays."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain what food I have to prepare or help prepare."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about things I have to but to get ready for the holiday."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about family life."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about future action, plans and intentions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about what is necessary. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you give gifts at Christmas or at other holidays? Only to family? To friends?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " If you could wish for anything at Christmas, what would it be? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_fe